{
 "id": "base-adapter-fdm",
 "brief": "An adapter that bolts my robot arm's base to a workbench. PETG, FDM, printed bottom down\n(layers along +Z). Four M5 screws go down into the bench along Z at (+/-40, +/-40); the bottom\n5 mm of the part (z = 0 to 5) must be solid in a 7 mm radius round each, with an M5 clearance\nhole, and I need a 10 mm diameter column clear straight above each screw for the socket. On top (z = 25 to 30)\nthere's a 90 mm OD / 60 mm ID ring that the arm's base bolts to with six M4 screws coming down\nfrom above on a 75 mm circle (first at +X, every 60 degrees) into heat-set inserts (6 mm hole,\n8 mm deep from the top). The centre (radius 30 mm) stays empty all the way through for cables.\nThe part fits in x and y of +/-48 and z = 0 to 30. The arm reaching out puts up to 6 N\u00b7m of\ntipping moment on the top ring, about any horizontal axis, plus 30 N of weight. Safety factor 2.",
 "attachments": [],
